{
  "_id": "6abb21e899f7aa8c6aa43448",
  "Package": "panoramic",
  "Title": "Variance-Aware Multi-Sample Spatial Colocalization Analysis",
  "Version": "0.99.4",
  "Authors@R": "person(\"Jacob\", \"Chang\", email = \"jachang4@stanford.edu\", role = c(\"aut\", \"cre\", \"fnd\"), comment = c(ORCID = \"0000-0002-3719-7949\"))",
  "Description": "Quantifies and compares cell-type spatial colocalization\nacross samples, patients, and conditions in spatial omics\nstudies. Its primary statistic, edge-corrected local\ncompetition enrichment, measures excess or deficit local mixing\nfor ordered cell-type pairs on a percentage-point scale. The\npackage estimates within-sample uncertainty with spatial\nbootstrap procedures and propagates it through multilevel\nrandom-effects meta-analysis for pooled inference and\ngroup-level contrasts; classical spatial summary statistics are\nalso supported.",
